  "interpretation": [
    "The blind 33/33/33 partition maps perfectly to U/G/B: U=unlinked, L1=Triple-Gear T(3,3), L2=Borromean.",
    "All 66 linked candidates pass the prospective 2+1 polarity gate; only two unlinked cells pass and their delta_cross is three orders of magnitude smaller than linked medians.",
    "Skeleton architecture dominates the measured linked-state observables; local 5_2/6_1 assignment and provider effects are orders of magnitude smaller in the linked factorial decomposition.",
    "Triple-Gear shows a repeatable knot-identity interaction: opposing a 6_1 component gives higher cross-stabilization in 23/24 historical mixed cells, including 12/12 uud-like cells where the lone 6_1 is opposed.",
    "Borromean shows no corresponding 5_2-vs-6_1 opposed-component preference (12/24 positive), indicating that its collective architecture largely washes out local twist-knot identity at this gate level.",
    "These results are reduced finite-core/Biot-Savart qualification results, not a derivation of proton/neutron identity, mass, charge, or full nonlinear stability."
  ],
  "caution": "Candidate cells share skeleton generators and provider anchors; treat classical p-values as descriptive only. v0.2 should use independent modal/Kelvin-Floquet and restoring-force validation rather than tune v0.1.1 thresholds after reveal."
